         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nIn previous classes, we learned how to count up to 10 using three symbols created by the Etruscan-Romans: I, V and X. But these are not their only numerical symbols.\n\nIn this class, we will learn how to use the symbols for 50 (L) and 100 (C), and how to write the numbers between them.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "66075b87-4bc1-486b-9806-a60ad666891e",
