               "uuid": "5fc193f7-7226-4852-82d1-706a44de71ec",
               "text": "The Missing Numbers",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=d603e3a0-cf2a-497d-9fc3-cfed73743515",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### It Is 10, Not 1\n\nTo write 40 as XL, we must use X (10) instead of I (1), because it is 10 units before 50 (L). The symbol placed before always has the same value as the group we are counting: in the tens, that value is 10, not 1.\n\nSee the numbers between 40 (XL) and 50 (L):",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p data-custom=\"etruscan-roman-tens-table-40-50\"></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Table 3: The numbers from 40 to 50.*",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "7d73642d-d579-4820-a026-a470bbd8d5e9",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
